$ (MSC's HA144B, antisymmetric, WKK = 2 I; the roll trim in subcase 1, the
$ divergence of listing 3-1 in subcase 2), cut to the derivative table and
$ the trim variables of subcase 1 and the complex eigenvalue and divergence
$ summaries of subcase 2. ROLL 8.541367E-02 is the plain deck's at q = 8.015
$ (WKK weights the trim's aerodynamics); the divergence roots are the plain
$ deck's to every digit (23.73470 ...): Simcenter's DIVERG does not weight
$ with WKK (scnas/nast/del/aestat.dat hands DIVERGRS the unweighted QKKS).
$ test_nastran95ase_trim_corrections.m holds nastran95ase to both.
